    <text>
        <front>
            <div type="summary">
                <p>
                    Typed copies of correspondence with Harcourt, Brace and Company regarding American rights in Virginia Woolf's works
                </p>
            </div>
        </front>
        <body>
            <div type="letter">
                <opener>
                    <dateline>
                        <placeName>
                           New York
                        </placeName>
                        <date when="1933-04-19">
                            April 19, 1933.
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                    <address>
                        <addrLine>
                            <persName key= "Q703935">Leonard Woolf</persName>, Esq.
                        </addrLine>
                        <addrLine>
                            52 Tavistock Square
                        </addrLine>
                         <addrLine>
                            London, W.C.l
                        </addrLine>
                    </address>
                    <salute>Dear Mr. Woolf:</salute>
                </opener>
                <p>
                I recieved yesterday your cable reading: <lb/>
                "Accept Atlantic Hogarth." Upon recieveng it, I telephoned <lb/>
                to <placeName>Boston</placeName> and talked with <persName>Mr. Sedgwick</persName> and succeded in <lb/>
                persuading him to push the price up to <!--dollar-->&#x24;1500.00. The sale of <lb/>
                the serial rights is therefore concluded at that figure. <lb/>
                I am sure you won't mind the additional sum, and the price <lb/>
                of &#x24;1500.00 seems more appropriate than the &#x24;1200.00 he offered. <lb/>
                </p>

                <p>
                I assume that you have gone ahead to set up <lb/>
                the book by this time, and I am hoping that we may receive <lb/>
                corrected proofs before long. It would be well to send us <lb/>
                two sets, one of which I might send on to the <orgName>Atlantic</orgName>. <lb/>
                No doubt, it will be better for them to print from the <lb/>
                corrected version if possible. Also, although book pub-<lb/>
                lication is put off until October, we shall still want as <lb/>
                complete samples as possible early in June. I should be <lb/>
                glad, therefore, if we might have the photographs you <lb/>
                select as soon as possible, as well as the corrected proofs: <lb/>
                or if the corrected proofs are to be long in coming, at <lb/>
                least the photographs.
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <salute>
                        With kind regards to you both,
                    </salute>
                    <salute>
                        Yours sincerely,
                    </salute>
                    <signed>Donald Brace</signed>
                    <seg>
                        DCB:CMc
                    </seg>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
